WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.244
Ben: Look out!

2
00:00:06.245 --> 00:00:09.317
Theo: That sheep keeps running away.

3
00:00:09.318 --> 00:00:15.289
Kyle: How can sheep be so fast?

4
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:20.492
Riley: They went through the gate. Finally!

5
00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:23.567
Mack: Sheep can be hard to herd.

6
00:00:23.568 --> 00:00:26.484
Mack: But they will stay in the pasture now.

7
00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:29.995
Mack: I fixed the fence.

8
00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:34.425
Sarah: Let's check the lamb again.

9
00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:37.074
Sarah: Is everything okay, Dr. May?

10
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:38.963
Dr. May: More than okay.

11
00:00:38.964 --> 00:00:44.214
Dr. May: Come here and take a look!

12
00:00:44.215 --> 00:00:46.907
Theo: There are two lambs!

13
00:00:46.908 --> 00:00:49.128
Theo: How did that happen?

14
00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:53.530
Dr. May: Sheep often have two babies.

15
00:00:53.531 --> 00:00:57.292
Riley: The little one has spots on her nose.

16
00:00:57.293 --> 00:01:00.053
Riley: We should call her Freckle!

17
00:01:00.054 --> 00:01:03.854
Skyler: The big one can be called Snowy.

18
00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:07.820
Skyler: Because he's so white.

19
00:01:07.821 --> 00:01:10.629
Mack: You kids did a good job today.

20
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.344
Mack: You helped the ewe.

21
00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:17.147
Mack: Paying attention to how animals act is important.

22
00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:24.519
Mack: It's a big part of taking care of them.

23
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.542
Riley: Hey, Snooks! Do you want to play fetch?

24
00:01:28.543 --> 00:01:32.267
Snooks: [i@Grr.@i]

25
00:01:32.268 --> 00:01:35.850
Riley: It's okay. I'm home now.

26
00:01:35.851 --> 00:01:40.699
Riley: But you still look really sad.

27
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.325
Riley's mom: He's been quiet again all day.

28
00:01:44.326 --> 00:01:47.321
Riley: Mom, you were right.

29
00:01:47.322 --> 00:01:51.206
Riley: Something is wrong with Snooks.

30
00:01:51.207 --> 00:01:56.503
Riley's mom: Let's take him to the vet.

31
00:01:56.504 --> 00:01:59.547
Dr. Hiller: Your dog has an ear infection.

32
00:01:59.548 --> 00:02:04.351
Dr. Hiller: Dogs with long ears get them sometimes.

33
00:02:04.352 --> 00:02:08.313
Dr. Hiller: But this medicine will make Snooks feel better.

34
00:02:08.314 --> 00:02:12.089
Riley: Poor Snooks. I'm sorry.

35
00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.368
Riley: I didn't notice how you were acting.

36
00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:22.451
Riley: From now on, I'll pay more attention to you!

37
00:02:22.452 --> 00:02:25.319
Snooks: [i@Ar-ooo!@i]

